  ('prompt_evolink_ui_103', 'evolink-ui-103-tropical-parrot-pixel-mosaic', 'Tropical Parrot Pixel Mosaic', 'A vibrant pixel-art style mosaic of a tropical parrot perched on a small brown branch in the middle of dense rainforest foliage. The entire image is rendered as a tight grid of tiny square tiles with visible black outlines, creating a stained-glass or LED-screen effect. The bird is shown in side profile facing right, with a large curved black beak, a pale cream face, a bright red-orange forehead and throat, vivid green upper body, and long wings and tail in saturated blue and cyan. The surrounding jungle is filled edge to edge with layered green leaves in many shades, with a soft light green glow behind the parrot to separate it from the background. High color contrast, rich tropical palette, crisp tile pattern, centered composition, decorative digital mosaic aesthetic.', 'UI mockup、社媒卡片、信息图和界面概念。来自 EvoLinkAI GPT-Image-2 案例库。', 'Tropical Parrot Pixel Mosaic UI mockup、社媒卡片、信息图和界面概念。来自 EvoLinkAI GPT-Image-2 案例库。 UI 与社媒 A vibrant pixel-art style mosaic of a tropical parrot perched on a small brown branch in the middle of dense rainforest foliage. The entire image is rendered as a tight grid of tiny square tiles with visible black outlines, creating a stained-glass or LED-screen effect. The bird is shown in side profile facing right, with a large curved black beak, a pale cream face, a bright red-orange forehead and throat, vivid green upper body, and long wings and tail in saturated blue and cyan. The surrounding jungle is filled edge to edge with layered green leaves in many shades, with a soft light green glow behind the parrot to separate it from the background. High color contrast, rich tropical palette, crisp tile pattern, centered composition, decorative digital mosaic aesthetic. @erikmackinnon EvoLinkAI GPT-Image 2 NanoBanan tag_ai_image tag_evolink tag_ui tag_design tag_mockup tag_3d tag_game tag_infographic', 'https://x.com/erikmackinnon/status/2048190288179675290', '@erikmackinnon', 'published', NULL, 5160, 510, 260, 1120, cast(unixepoch('subsecond') * 1000 as integer), cast(unixepoch('subsecond') * 1000 as integer), cast(unixepoch('subsecond') * 1000 as integer));
