  ('prompt_youm_53', 'youmind-53-infographic-edu-visual-ink-wash-style-presentation-slides', 'Infographic / Edu Visual - Ink-Wash Style Presentation Slides', 'Title: {argument name="Title" default="Enter slide title here"}
INSERT INTO `prompts` (`id`, `slug`, `title`, `content`, `description`, `search_text`, `source_url`, `source_author`, `status`, `author_id`, `view_count`, `like_count`, `collect_count`, `copy_count`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `published_at`)
VALUES
  ('prompt_youm_54', 'youmind-54-infographic-edu-visual-misordered-image-relay-grid', 'Infographic / Edu Visual - Misordered Image Relay Grid', 'Based on the attached image, arrange {argument name="quantity" default="12 versions"} in a {argument name="grid" default="3x4"} grid. Express this as if the image were passed sequentially to 12 different people, each looking only at what the previous person made and mistakenly assuming ''this must be what was requested'' or ''this is meant for this purpose,'' leading them to redesign it. Start the first frame with an atmosphere very close to the original. As the frames progress, have the shape, color, expression, pose, composition, motifs, and mood of the original image gradually be misunderstood, simplified, converted for different uses, and move away from its original meaning and appearance. Each frame should look like it was remade by a person who only saw the previous frame and judged ''this must have been the request.'' Naturally change it according to the content of the original image, whether it''s a person, character, pet, food, landscape, building, or profile image. Do not fix the intermediate changes too strictly. It''s okay to misunderstand it as an illustration in one frame, a mascot in the next, a commercial product, a sign, a flyer, a stuffed toy, food packaging, tourist goods, a warning sign, a game character, a mysterious toy, a reference icon, or a handmade craft. The direction of change should be naturally associated with the appearance of the original and the previous frame. As the frames progress, make it look like ''you can tell someone was trying to make it properly, but they slightly misunderstood what the request was.'' Let the shapes, proportions, eyes, mouths, outlines, color placement, textures, uses, decorations, and compositions shift bit by bit, leading to an unexpected and humorous appearance in the latter half. The key is not just image degradation or noise, but to make it look like it''s collapsing because humans misinterpreted the previous result while rebuilding it for a different purpose. In the latter half, do not completely erase the characteristics of the original image, but unnaturally leave one or two elements like color, outline, expression, hairstyle, clothes, accessories, pose, composition, or motif. Meanwhile, other elements can be boldly omitted, transformed, misunderstood, or turned into something else. Make the 12th frame bold enough that only someone who knows the original image can barely sense the original source, while appearing as a completely different mysterious entity, product, character, craft, icon, or mascot to a first-time viewer. End with an unexpected and slightly funny landing that makes people think ''Why did it end up like this?!'' Make each frame look different. Keep the background white and simple, organized into a 3x4 grid for easy viewing of the 12 variations. In the later frames, don''t make them too neat; instead, let one person''s misunderstanding be further misunderstood by the next. In the 12th frame, change it so boldly that while one feature of the original remains strangely, everything else is almost entirely different.', 'A complex creative prompt that transforms an input image through 12 stages of intentional ''misinterpretation'' by imaginary sequential creators, resulting in a humorous 3x4 evolution grid.。来自 YouMind-OpenLab GPT-Image-2 案例库。', 'Infographic / Edu Visual - Misordered Image Relay Grid A complex creative prompt that transforms an input image through 12 stages of intentional ''misinterpretation'' by imaginary sequential creators, resulting in a humorous 3x4 evolution grid.。来自 YouMind-OpenLab GPT-Image-2 案例库。 Based on the attached image, arrange {argument name="quantity" default="12 versions"} in a {argument name="grid" default="3x4"} grid. Express this as if the image were passed sequentially to 12 different people, each looking only at what the previous person made and mistakenly assuming ''this must be what was requested'' or ''this is meant for this purpose,'' leading them to redesign it. Start the first frame with an atmosphere very close to the original. As the frames progress, have the shape, color, expression, pose, composition, motifs, and mood of the original image gradually be misunderstood, simplified, converted for different uses, and move away from its original meaning and appearance. Each frame should look like it was remade by a person who only saw the previous frame and judged ''this must have been the request.'' Naturally change it according to the content of the original image, whether it''s a person, character, pet, food, landscape, building, or profile image. Do not fix the intermediate changes too strictly. It''s okay to misunderstand it as an illustration in one frame, a mascot in the next, a commercial product, a sign, a flyer, a stuffed toy, food packaging, tourist goods, a warning sign, a game character, a mysterious toy, a reference icon, or a handmade craft. The direction of change should be naturally associated with the appearance of the original and the previous frame. As the frames progress, make it look like ''you can tell someone was trying to make it properly, but they slightly misunderstood what the request was.'' Let the shapes, proportions, eyes, mouths, outlines, color placement, textures, uses, decorations, and compositions shift bit by bit, leading to an unexpected and humorous appearance in the latter half. The key is not just image degradation or noise, but to make it look like it''s collapsing because humans misinterpreted the previous result while rebuilding it for a different purpose. In the latter half, do not completely erase the characteristics of the original image, but unnaturally leave one or two elements like color, outline, expression, hairstyle, clothes, accessories, pose, composition, or motif. Meanwhile, other elements can be boldly omitted, transformed, misunderstood, or turned into something else. Make the 12th frame bold enough that only someone who knows the original image can barely sense the original source, while appearing as a completely different mysterious entity, product, character, craft, icon, or mascot to a first-time viewer. End with an unexpected and slightly funny landing that makes people think ''Why did it end up like this?!'' Make each frame look different. Keep the background white and simple, organized into a 3x4 grid for easy viewing of the 12 variations. In the later frames, don''t make them too neat; instead, let one person''s misunderstanding be further misunderstood by the next. In the 12th frame, change it so boldly that while one feature of the original remains strangely, everything else is almost entirely different. やげん✨🐎｜推しの為にAIを極めるおっさん社会人 YouMind-OpenLab GPT-Image 2 NanoBanan tag_ai_image tag_youmind tag_food tag_poster tag_ui tag_logo tag_game tag_sticker', 'https://x.com/rascal8023/status/2052946911813099889', 'やげん✨🐎｜推しの為にAIを極めるおっさん社会人', 'published', NULL, 2514, 216, 113, 532, cast(unixepoch('subsecond') * 1000 as integer), cast(unixepoch('subsecond') * 1000 as integer), cast(unixepoch('subsecond') * 1000 as integer));
